 "description": "A juvenile Belatz: 2 body regions (B2), a head, 2 eyes, a 2-leaf crest, 2 legs, 2 flaps, a tail; feathers; upright, neck head. Coat: colour cobalt and lagoon; fluff short and straight; sheen between; feathers between; fur reach bushy tail; second colour butter and ice. Face: head between; beak short; crest between; crown low; eyes between. Shape: waist thick; back line level; hind body between; body barrel; build between. Legs & tail: tail curl straight; tail between. Proportions: a large body, the head carried high, a short beak, a low crest, long legs, broad feet, a thick waist, wide flaps. Posture: standing upright on its two legs, weight on its broad feet, body held level, still, looking at the viewer.",
